        "original_id": "e055fcea-e04e-502e-bd69-98136cf65f3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: My Darkest Days, Human Drama\n- People: Matt Walst, Brendan McMillan, Doug Oliver, Reid Henry, Johnny Indovina, Mark Henry Balderas\n- Songs: \"Casual Sex\"\n- Places: Peterborough, Ontario; Encino, California\n\nFacts:\n- Human Drama is an American alternative rock band formed in 1985 and led by singer-songwriter Johnny Indovina.\n- Mark Henry Balderas was born on September 10, 1959, in Encino, California.\n- Mark Henry Balderas was the keyboard player for Human Drama from 1986 to 1991, again from 1993 to 2005, and again from 2012 to 2017.\n- Human Drama released six studio albums before splitting in 2005, and Johnny Indovina was its only constant member.\n- My Darkest Days were a Canadian rock band based in Peterborough, Ontario, with Matt Walst, Brendan McMillan, Doug Oliver, and Reid Henry as members.\n- \"Casual Sex\" is a song by the Canadian rock band My Darkest Days.",
